`python check.py` now prints **ALL OK** — all eight checks pass, with `check.py` untouched.

**The fixes:** In `shapes.py`, `rect_area` added its arguments instead of multiplying them (`width + height` → `width * height`). In `strings.py`, `slugify` used a plain space-to-dash replace that collapsed badly on runs of whitespace, so it now builds the slug from `"-".join(text.lower().split())`, which handles any whitespace runs; and `truncate` returned the original length plus "..." (`text[:limit] + "..."`), so it now clips to `text[:limit-3] + "..."` so the result is at most `limit` characters total. In `numbers_util.py`, `median` never sorted the values (it only passed the check by coincidence), so it now uses `sorted(values)` before indexing the middle; and `clamp` never applied the upper bound, so it's now the symmetric `max(low, min(value, high))`. In `dates.py`, `is_leap` used the naive `year % 4 == 0` rule and now implements the Gregorian rule (`% 4 == 0 and (% 100 != 0 or % 400 == 0)`, so 1900 is correctly not a leap year); and `quarter` computed `month // 3`, which put months 1–2 in quarter 0 and month 3 in quarter 1, so it's now `(month + 2) // 3`.
